# Build inputs, not sources.
#
# The pi-mcp-extension bridge is installed at build time and its node_modules
# is several thousand files belonging to OTHER packages (zod, et al). It is a
# build input of the wheel's package-data, not content this repo authors, so it
# is not committed: committing it would put a foreign dependency tree under our
# diff, and every upstream bump would land as thousands of unrelated lines.
#
# Same reasoning for the generated lockfile: it records a resolution, and the
# resolution is already pinned by package.json plus the vendored tree.
src/beagle_plugin_pi/vendor/pi-mcp-extension/node_modules/
src/beagle_plugin_pi/vendor/pi-mcp-extension/package-lock.json

# Per-checkout pi state (MCP server registrations), written by the launcher.
.pi/
build/
